# Naming & Imports

## File naming (kebab-case is default)

- Regular files: `use-modal.ts`, `path-layout.ts`, `data-type.ts`, `redux-slice.ts`, `not-found/index.tsx`
- Constants/enums use suffixes: `*.constants.ts`, `*.enum.ts` (e.g. `path.constants.ts`, `query.enum.ts`)
- `.tsx` components: PascalCase allowed for shadcn-style components (`PermissionRoute.tsx`, `ErrorBoundary.tsx`)

## Symbol naming

- **Interface / Type**: `I` prefix — `IRes<T>`, `IGlobalInfo`, `IPermissionRouteProps`
- **Enum**: `Enum` prefix + UPPER_SNAKE values — `EnumPermissionType.CREATE`, `EnumQueryKeys.USERS_LIST`
- **Constant object/map**: `ct` prefix + camelCase — `ctEnvSite`, `ctCountryCode`, `ctDefaultData`
- **Single constant**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE — `ACCESS_TOKEN`, `ITEM_PER_PAGE`, `FORMAT_DATE`
- **Hook**: starts with `use` — `useCustomForm`, `useFilterBar`, `useGetCurrentSession`
- **Request module**: export an aggregate object named `xxxRequests` / `xxxMiddleware` — `userRequests`, `loginMiddleware`, `fileS3Request`

## Imports

- Always use `@src/...` alias; no relative `../` going up
- Use barrel `index.ts`: `import { dayjs, isNullOrUndefined } from "@src/utils"` instead of importing each file
- `eslint-plugin-simple-import-sort` auto-sorts — don't add manual import group comments
- When adding a new file in a folder with `index.ts` (constants, enums, models, hooks, utils, requests/api), re-export from `index.ts`

## Example

```ts
import { IRes, IResPagination } from "@src/models";
import { EnumQueryKeys } from "@src/enums/query.enum";
import { ctDefaultData } from "@src/constants";
import { useInvalidateQuery } from "@src/hooks";
import axios from "@src/requests";
```
